      "summary": "What happens to one proposed change to one content block: drafted, validated mechanically and by review, shown to the editor, and committed to the corpus only if accepted.",
      "description": "What happens to one proposed change to one content block: drafted, validated mechanically and by review, shown to the editor, and committed to the corpus only if accepted. folio-assistant — editing a content block and its HCI validation gate.\nSource of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other\nBPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it\nby `bun run render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.\nThe <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill\nthat implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared\nwork plan in beans/.",
